Pointer moves and resizes follow the window they began on, not focus.

kwm looked the window up through focus on every op_delta and op_release and
treated a focused window without an operation as unreachable, so a window
opening or closing mid-drag, or a tag switch, aborted kwm and took the session
down with it. A release after focus moved never ended the operation either,
and a window closed mid-drag left the seat in it.

